---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contrail check extension — privacy policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Contrail check for Google Flights browser extension."
  noindex
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[680px] px-6 py-12">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-3">
      Browser extension
    </p>
    <h1>Contrail check — privacy policy</h1>
    <p>
      The Contrail check for Google Flights extension adds predicted
      contrail-warming estimates to flight search results. It is built and
      operated by the Sustainable Solutions Lab at Stanford University.
    </p>
    <h2>What the extension does with data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        It reads the flight details displayed on Google Flights results
        pages you visit (airports, dates, departure times, layovers) and
        sends only those schedule details to our prediction service
        (sustainablesolutions.vercel.app) to compute warming estimates.
      </li>
      <li>
        It does not collect, store, or transmit any personal information,
        account details, browsing history, or page content beyond the
        flight schedule details above.
      </li>
      <li>
        It sets no cookies and keeps no local data. Our service does not
        log identifying information with prediction requests.
      </li>
      <li>It contains no ads, analytics, or third-party trackers.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Questions: contact the Sustainable Solutions Lab via
      <a href="https://sustainablesolutions.stanford.edu">sustainablesolutions.stanford.edu</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
